WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Now, let's talk about burn injuries.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.720
Burns can happen in an instant, whether from the sun, hot liquids, electricity, or chemicals.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:14.400
Before we look at the degrees, remember that any burn on the face, hands, feet, or genitals,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.959
or any burn larger than two to three inches, needs to be evaluated by a healthcare professional

00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:20.200
immediately.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.040
If someone's clothing is on fire, have them stop, drop, and roll immediately, and use

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.879
a blanket or water to smother the flames.

00:00:27.879 --> 00:00:30.680
Once the fire is out, call 911.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.560
We categorize burns by how deep the damage goes.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.959
First degree burns.

00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:38.840
These are superficial, like a typical sunburn.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:42.080
The skin is red, painful, and swollen.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:47.080
To treat this, rinse the area with cool running water for 10 to 20 minutes until the pain

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.240
subsides, then cover it with a non-stick dressing.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.759
Second degree burns.

00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:57.439
These go deeper and are very painful, often appearing blotchy with blisters.

00:00:57.439 --> 00:00:58.720
It is the same.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.639
Cool water for 10 to 20 minutes and a non-stick dressing, but it is vital that you do not

00:01:03.639 --> 00:01:07.919
pop the blisters, as they protect the skin while it heals.

00:01:07.919 --> 00:01:09.800
Third degree burns.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:15.199
These are severe, full-thickness burns where the skin may look charred, white, or leathery,

00:01:15.199 --> 00:01:17.839
potentially exposing fat or muscle.

00:01:17.839 --> 00:01:22.199
Paradoxically, these may be less painful if the nerves have been damaged.

00:01:22.199 --> 00:01:27.080
When providing care for severe burns, do not remove any clothing that is stuck to the skin,

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:32.320
though you should gently remove jewelry or loose clothing before swelling makes it difficult.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.639
Cover the area with a clean, dry dressing, and keep the person warm to prevent shock.

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:43.040
Most importantly, never apply butter, ointments, or home remedies to a severe burn, and do

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.480
not immerse large burns in water, as this can interfere with medical treatment.

